{
  "id": "E03",
  "title": "Middleware Pulse",
  "content": "<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.12) 0%, rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.04) 100%); border: 1px solid rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.2); border-left: 4px solid #EAB308; padding: 32px; margin-bottom: 60px; border-radius: 4px; position: relative; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"position: absolute; top: -20px; right: -20px; opacity: 0.05; transform: rotate(15deg);\"><svg width=\"120\" height=\"120\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#EAB308\" stroke-width=\"1\"><path d=\"M22 12h-4l-3 9L9 3l-3 9H2\"/></svg></div><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-heading); font-weight: 300;\">Master the <strong>Middleware Pulse</strong>. Learn to orchestrate complex request life-cycles using Photon's non-blocking, recursive pipeline architecture.</p></div><h2>The Execution Lifecycle</h2><p>Middleware in Photon follows a strict symmetrical execution pattern. Every interceptor can act as a gatekeeper, a transformer, or a post-processor.</p><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; margin: 48px 0;\" class=\"bento-grid\"><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(234,179,8,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"> <div style=\"color: #EAB308; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"13 17 18 12 13 7\"/><polyline points=\"6 17 11 12 6 7\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">INGRESS</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Logic executed <strong>Before</strong> the handler. Ideal for Auth, Rate Limiting, and Body Parsing.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(234,179,8,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"><div style=\"color: #EAB308; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"11 17 6 12 11 7\"/><polyline points=\"18 17 13 12 18 7\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">EGRESS</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Logic executed <strong>After</strong> the handler. Used for Logging, Compression, and Header Injection.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(234,179,8,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"><div style=\"color: #EAB308; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><line x1=\"15\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"9\" y2=\"15\"/><line x1=\"9\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"15\" y2=\"15\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">HALT</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Early returns that break the chain. Prevents downstream execution in unauthorized scenarios.</p></div></div><h2>Middleware Topology</h2><p>From global monitoring to path-specific security, the Pulse API allows for granular control over every network segment.</p><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px; margin: 40px 0;\"><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 24px; border-radius: 4px;\"><h4 style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 800; color: #D1D5DB; text-transform: uppercase;\">Global Pulse</h4><pre style=\"margin:0; padding:0; background:transparent; font-size:11px;\"><code>// Monitoring for every request\napp.use(async (c, next) => {\n  const start = performance.now()\n  await next()\n  const ms = performance.now() - start\n  c.header('X-Pulse-Time', `${ms}ms`)\n})</code></pre></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 24px; border-radius: 4px;\"><h4 style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 800; color: #D1D5DB; text-transform: uppercase;\">Scoped Security</h4><pre style=\"margin:0; padding:0; background:transparent; font-size:11px;\"><code>// Targeted gatekeeping\napp.use('/admin/*', async (c, next) => {\n  const auth = c.req.header('Auth')\n  if (!auth) return c.unauthorized()\n  await next()\n})</code></pre></div></div><div style=\"background: rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.05); border: 1px solid rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.1); border-left: 4px solid #EAB308; padding: 24px; margin: 40px 0; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;\"><h4 style=\"margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 900; color: #EAB308; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;\">// PULSE_INSIGHT: REUSABILITY</h4><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-style: italic; color: var(--text-heading); opacity: 0.9; border: none; padding: 0;\">Use <strong>Factory Functions</strong> to generate middleware with dynamic configurations, such as rate limits or environment-specific logging levels.</p></div><h2>Architecture Best Practices</h2><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 2fr); gap: 20px; margin: 40px 0;\" class=\"bento-grid\"><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 24px; border-radius: 4px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 12px 0; color: #10B981;\">✓ ALWAYS NEXT</h3><p style=\"font-size: 13px; opacity: 0.8; margin: 0;\">Ensure <code>await next()</code> is called unless you intend to halt the request. Losing the trace is losing the response.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 24px; border-radius: 4px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 12px 0; color: #10B981;\">✓ ORDER MATTERS</h3><p style=\"font-size: 13px; opacity: 0.8; margin: 0;\">Registration order determines the nesting. Place expensive IO operations closer to the core handler.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 24px; border-radius: 4px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 12px 0; color: #10B981;\">✓ CONTEXT SHARING</h3><p style=\"font-size: 13px; opacity: 0.8; margin: 0;\">Use <code>c.get()</code> and <code>c.set()</code> to share request-scoped data instead of modifying the global state.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 24px; border-radius: 4px;\"><h3 style=\"font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 12px 0; color: #10B981;\">✓ TRY-CATCH WRAPPING</h3><p style=\"font-size: 13px; opacity: 0.8; margin: 0;\">Global error handlers should be the first layer in the Pulse, catching any downstream failures gracefully.</p></div></div>",
